sed on the unaudited 2025/26 final accounts. The paper's reserves schedule uses the same unaudited opening balances.","iso":"2026-11-24","paper_title":"10 Budget Monitoring Update 2026 27 Quarter 2","paper_url":"https://northeast-ca.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s1922/1922.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"The Investment Fund is forecast at \u00a353.372m against a \u00a358.454m budget, a net underspend of \u00a35.082m","lead":"Revenue spend is forecast below budget and capital spend above budget. The paper says the capital forecast includes an element of overprogramming, which will be managed within the Investment Fund's medium-term resources and reserve balances.","iso":"2026-11-24","paper_title":"10 Budget Monitoring Update 2026 27 Quarter 2","paper_url":"https://northeast-ca.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s1922/1922.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-11-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"10 Budget Monitoring Update 2026 27 Quarter 2","paper_url":"https://northeast-ca.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s1922/1922.pdf","headline":"Employee costs are forecast below budget because of vacancies held longer than planned","detail":"The paper says the in-year cost of colleagues who joined part-way through the year will result in a higher cost for 2027/28, because a full year's salary costs will then be incurred.","category":"people","matters":"A vacancy saving in 2026/27 that reverses into a higher cost in 2027/28 is a timing effect a finance director would want to see carried into the next year's budget.","figures":"\u00a30.6m underspend against budgeted staffing costs; \u00a30.603m employees variance in Table 2","quote":"a \u00a30.6m underspend against budgeted staffing costs","read_on":"2026-11-18","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"10 Budget Monitoring Update 2026 27 Quarter 2","paper_url":"https://northeast-ca.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s1922/1922.pdf","headline":"Reserve figures rest on unaudited 2025/26 final accounts","detail":"The paper asks Cabinet to note the reserves value, which is based on the unaudited 2025/26 final accounts. The paper's reserves schedule uses the same unaudited opening balances.","category":"audit","matters":"A finance director or lender would note that the opening reserve balances are not yet audited, so the forecast closing balance depends on them.","figures":"\u00a3501.7m opening usable reserves based on unaudited accounts","quote":"based on the unaudited 2025/26 final accounts for the North East Mayoral Strategic Authority","read_on":"2026-11-18","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"10 Budget Monitoring Update 2026 27 Quarter 2","paper_url":"https://northeast-ca.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s1922/1922.pdf","headline":"The Investment Fund is forecast at \u00a353.372m against a \u00a358.454m budget, a net underspend of \u00a35.082m","detail":"Revenue spend is forecast below budget and capital spend above budget. The paper says the capital forecast includes an element of overprogramming, which will be managed within the Investment Fund's medium-term resources and reserve balances.","category":"capital","matters":"Capital overprogramming funded from reserves is a choice other finance directors would compare with their own medium-term resource planning.","figures":"\u00a353.372m forecast vs \u00a358.454m budget; \u00a35.082m net underspend","quote":"representing a net underspend of \u00a35.082m","read_on":"2026-11-18","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"10 Budget Monitoring Update 2026 27 Quarter 2","paper_url":"https://northeast-ca.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s1922/1922.pdf","headline":"Investment balances rose from \u00a3451.0m to \u00a3771.3m, after receipt of \u00a3417m of Integrated Settlement grant in April 2026","detail":"Investments are held across banks (\u00a3610.0m), other local authorities (\u00a370.0m) and money market funds (\u00a391.267m), with no balances in the Debt Management Office. The paper says the balances are invested to prioritise security and liquidity before yield.","category":"other","matters":"A large cash balance from an upfront grant payment is a counterparty and liquidity exposure a lender and treasury officer would track.","figures":"\u00a3451.0m at 1 April 2026; \u00a3771.3m at 30 September 2026; \u00a3417m Integrated Settlement grant; banks \u00a3610.0m; other local authorities \u00a370.0m; money market funds \u00a391.267m","quote":"Investment balances increased from \u00a3451.0m at the start of the year to \u00a3771.3m at 30 September 2026","read_on":"2026-11-18","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-24","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"10 Budget Monitoring Update 2026 27 Quarter 2","paper_url":"https://northeast-ca.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s1922/1922.pdf","headline":"External borrowing is \u00a3113.0m at 30 September 2026, with no new borrowing or early repayment in the first six months","detail":"The portfolio comprises \u00a378.0m of PWLB borrowing and \u00a335.0m of private sector borrowing. The paper records a scheduled PWLB repayment of \u00a30.333m in Q2. The paper says the Authority remained within all approved treasury management indicators.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A council holding a stable debt portfolio with no early repayments or new borrowing is a position a lender would read directly from the treasury update.","figures":"\u00a3113.0m external borrowing; \u00a378.0m PWLB; \u00a335.0m private sector; \u00a30.333m scheduled repayment; average rates 4.10% (PWLB) and 4.21% (private sector)","quote":"There has been no new borrowing taken out or early repayment of borrowing during the first six months of the financial year","read_on":"2026-11-18","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-11-24"},"name":"North East Mayoral Combined Authority","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-11-25","since_iso":"2026-10-26","distress":false,"headline":"Employee costs are forecast below budget because of vacancies held longer than planned","lead":"A vacancy saving in 2026/27 that reverses into a higher cost in 2027/28 is a timing effect a finance director would want to see carried into the next year's budget.","also":["20 other findings in this window","15 papers caught"],"watch":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee on 2026-12-08","n_findings":21,"n_documents":15,"top_paper_title":"10 Budget Monitoring Update 2026 27 Quarter 2","top_paper_url":"https://northeast-ca.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s1922/1922.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":43,"news_drafts_total":3}}